    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac23<x<1$.\n\nApply the triangle inequality to all three side pairs and intersect the bounds.",
      "worked": "Each pair of sides must sum to more than the remaining side.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x-1)+(3x+2)&>5-x\\\\5x+1&>5-x\\\\6x&>4\\\\x&>\\frac23\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x-1)+(5-x)&>3x+2\\\\x+4&>3x+2\\\\2&>2x\\\\x&<1\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(3x+2)+(5-x)&>2x-1\\\\2x+7&>2x-1\\\\7&>-1\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe third inequality is always true. Combining the first two gives $\\frac23<x<1$. Throughout this interval, $2x-1>\\frac13$, $3x+2>4$ and $5-x>4$, so all three side lengths are positive.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
